Sure, initializing the GPIO on an ESP32 is straightforward. Here's a simple function to do that:

```c
#include "driver/gpio.h"

void gpio_init() {
    // Set GPIO0 as an output
    gpio_set_direction(GPIO_NUM_0, GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT);
}
```

This function sets GPIO0 to be an output, which is a common initial setup for many ESP32 projects.
